course: dictionary
lesson: 1944
title: What is a commitment?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A commitment is something you have decided to do and will keep doing, even when it is hard. «Her commitment to the team meant she came to every practice, even in the rain.» Commitment shows loyalty: you stick with something because you care about it.
explain: A commitment can also be a promise or a duty you have agreed to. «I have other commitments on Saturday» means you have already promised to be somewhere or do something, so you cannot come. Other people rely on you to keep it.
explain: Commitment can also mean something that takes up your time or money. To work out the meaning, ask: is this about hard work, a promise, or time and money? Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Commitment is a noun: a commitment, commitments.
fact: «Commitment» means working hard, sticking with something and being loyal to it.
fact: «A promise is a commitment that another person relies on.»
fact: In the Ramayana, Rama goes into exile, sent away to live far from home, to keep his father's word.
fact: Joshua made a public commitment: «As for me and my household, we will serve the Lord.»
exercise: «Her commitment to the team meant she came to every practice.» What does commitment mean here? | *Working hard and staying loyal to something | A free ticket to a match | Losing a game | Dislike of the coach
exercise: «I have other commitments on Saturday.» What does commitment mean here? | A type of football boot | *A promise or duty you have agreed to | A colour of the sky
exercise: Which of these is a commitment that takes up time? | Reading a comic | Eating breakfast | *Going to a swimming club every Tuesday evening
test: «Joshua said, "As for me and my household, we will serve the Lord": a public commitment.» Why is this a commitment? | Because he was tired | *Because he promised it in front of others | Because it was a joke | Because it was a song
test: What does «fulfil every commitment» ask you to do? | Forget what you agreed | Make new friends | *Keep your promises and duties | Ask for more money
exam: What does commitment mean in «A promise is a commitment that another person relies on»? | *A promise or duty others count on | A type of food | A colour | A game
